  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "Model serialisation is the process of converting a trained machine learning model \u2014 including its architecture definition, learned weights, and associated metadata \u2014 into a persistent, portable file format that can be stored, transferred, and subsequently loaded to restore the model to an operational state. Serialisation enables reproducibility, deployment across different environments, and sharing of pre-trained models through repositories. Common formats include ONNX for cross-framework portability, SafeTensors for security, PyTorch checkpoint files, and framework-native formats such as TensorFlow SavedModel.",
